      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "So I am not sure if it was a Proton update, or a VRChat update, or whatever, but the font issue is gone for me. I can see japanese names just fine now.\nEDIT: It was a Proton update. https://github.com/ValveSoftware/Proton/releases/tag/proton-4.11-3",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-07-27T12:54:20.537Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Adding additional fallbacks for the fonts used in VRChat, would allow users to still see all names and menus properly, even without having the current restrictive fonts installed.\nIn practice, this would allow Linux users to see non english characters (e.g. Japanese).\n\nFallback fonts that I would suggest, would be: \nBank Gothic -> \"Ume P Gothic\"(for Ubuntu), \"UmePlus P Gothic\"(for Mandriva), \"Takao P Gothic\"\n\nDosis (is available for Linux) -> \"UnDotum\"(for Ubuntu), \"DroidSansFallbackFull\"\n\nOf course fonts could also just be shipped with VRChat.\n\nDocumentation on fallback fonts is available here: https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/class-Font.html",
